<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>BBC News</title><subtitle type="html">BBC News - Technology</subtitle><id>https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/technology/rss.xml</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:09:12Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss.xml" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/technology" /><link rel="via" href="https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/technology/rss.xml" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Pensions and benefits services still down after 'cyber incident'</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm1wrgqyq4d8o#0</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:07:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-28T07:55:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm1wrgqyq4d8o--6811ba22810e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm1wrgqyq4d8o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The UK's former chief technology officer says the Department for Work and Pensions may have been hit by hackers, but the government has not confirmed that.</summary></entry><entry><title>How gamers are using AI and leaked files to clone Grand Theft Auto 6</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c64gn8pe5eeqo#0</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:07:35Z</updated><published>2026-11-28T01:30:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c64gn8pe5eeqo--bb0be17c4eef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c64gn8pe5eeqo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">With an official PC version potentially still months away, fans are getting impatient.</summary></entry><entry><title>Why is there a shortage of 'wizard' elevator mechanics?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c52e8k19y94mo#0</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:35Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T00:02:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c52e8k19y94mo--3c01055c44d7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c52e8k19y94mo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The pay is good and there's lots of work, so what's behind the shortage of elevator mechanics?</summary></entry><entry><title>Asia made a big AI bet on Nvidia. What happens now?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqevr4lnd1nxo#0</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:35Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T23:08:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqevr4lnd1nxo--1319dbd59774.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqevr4lnd1nxo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Asian stocks have been on a rollercoaster ride after Jensen Huang's shock return as Nvidia CEO.</summary></entry><entry><title>Musk's plan to send a million SpaceX data satellites into space approved</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwp836l8n1jgo#0</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:35Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T09:27:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwp836l8n1jgo--29f2b2d83a49.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwp836l8n1jgo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The Starmind constellation aims to be the most cost and energy-efficient way to meet the growing demand for AI computing power.</summary></entry><entry><title>Huawei found guilty of stealing US trade secrets but acquitted of racketeering</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmy49ngydqzpo#0</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:35Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T10:52:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmy49ngydqzpo--762ce6d7fedd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmy49ngydqzpo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The verdict follows a months-long trial in New York.</summary></entry><entry><title>EA adds AI-generated John Motson to FC 27 video game</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c65y10j841jpo#0</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:35Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T10:11:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c65y10j841jpo--b50e46d04304.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c65y10j841jpo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The AI-generated Motson will appear in the game on 26 November, with the consent of his son and wife.</summary></entry><entry><title>Zoe Kleinman: Nobody is irreplaceable - unless you're Jensen Huang</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c3rrgqj2zx5yo#0</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:35Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T10:03:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c3rrgqj2zx5yo--58957c3acc4b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c3rrgqj2zx5yo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The BBC's technology and AI editor on how Nvidia's boss made himself impossible to fire.</summary></entry><entry><title>US attorney general dodges questions about Nvidia investigation</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/crpdw1qx7jgxo#0</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:35Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T03:44:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/crpdw1qx7jgxo--2a1422ea57bb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/crpdw1qx7jgxo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Nvidia's share price have fallen 7% as lawmakers demand answers about President Donald Trump's involvement in Huang's reinstatement.</summary></entry><entry><title>Why tiny cars are taking off across Europe</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmwy9jne0g7qo#0</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:35Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T00:34:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmwy9jne0g7qo--3267b6051ed1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmwy9jne0g7qo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Once seen as a car for elderly, rural people, tiny cars are being embraced by a younger demographic.</summary></entry><entry><title>Faisal Islam: Fears over the AI boom haven't gone away</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6894evgpel5o#0</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:35Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T18:21:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6894evgpel5o--a4e986911abd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6894evgpel5o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">There were legitimate fears before Huang's abrupt exit from Nvidia - and his return won't fix it</summary></entry><entry><title>Helpful but awkward: My week with Meta's Muse ahead of its UK launch</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c9gkld2l38y6o#0</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:35Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T09:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c9gkld2l38y6o--217d643100a8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c9gkld2l38y6o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Meta wants Muse to do for AI what WhatsApp did for messaging - here's what the BBC's technology editor found when she used it.</summary></entry><entry><title>US to blacklist Asian AI firm Megaspeed after Nvidia scandal</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cv98xpg5dg5zo#0</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:35Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T23:16:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../